00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.092
I assume you already have one.

00:02:22.092 --> 00:02:23.671
'Cause you won't enjoy it.

00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:26.730
Yeah, when we set out to write this thing,

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:29.433
and we defined what mythicality meant.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.323
Which you know what?

00:02:32.323 --> 00:02:33.310
I'm gonna read it.

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:36.470
The quality or state of being
that embodies a synergistic

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.937
coalescence of curiosity,
creativity, and tomfoolery,

00:02:40.937 --> 00:02:43.680
sometimes referred to as curio tomfoolery.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.656
I didn't even say that right,
sometimes referred to as

00:02:45.656 --> 00:02:47.780
Curiotomfoolivity.

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:48.613
Foolivity.

00:02:49.911 --> 00:02:52.893
Ideally experienced in
the context of friendship,

00:02:52.893 --> 00:02:56.293
and intended to bring
goodwill to the universe.

00:02:56.293 --> 00:02:58.351
We worked on that definition
for quite some time.

00:02:58.351 --> 00:03:01.660
And we worked on this
book for a long time.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.990
That's what we're about y'all.

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.270
If you wanna know what Rhett
and Link's about, that's it.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.394
It's about curiotomfoolivity.

00:03:07.394 --> 00:03:08.233
Right.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.890
And we dedicated this book
in memory of Ben Greenwood.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:17.890
His friendship changed our
lives, but ended way too soon.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.581
And there's a picture of
the three of us together

00:03:20.581 --> 00:03:22.390
right there.

